course: dictionary
lesson: 842
title: Berries: sweet, safe and sometimes deadly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A berry is a small round juicy fruit with seeds, like a blueberry or raspberry. «Many berries that look tasty are poisonous, and some are dangerous even in small amounts.» So a shiny berry can look lovely and still be dangerous.
explain: Scientists use a stricter meaning. A berry is a fruit made from one flower, with seeds inside its soft flesh. By that rule, «a banana is a berry but a strawberry is not», and grapes and tomatoes count too.
explain: Never eat a wild berry unless an adult who knows says it is safe. «A boy in Scotland ate shiny red berries from a bush in the park; he was sick and dizzy, and his mum had to rush him to hospital.» Holly, yew and mistletoe berries are all poisonous.
fact: A berry is a small round juicy fruit with seeds.
fact: Blueberries, raspberries and strawberries are all fruits people call berries.
fact: In science, a berry is a fruit made from one flower with seeds inside its soft flesh.
fact: By the science rule, bananas and grapes are berries, but strawberries are not.
fact: Birds and animals eat berries and drop the seeds far away, so new plants can grow.
fact: Many wild berries are poisonous, because plants use poisons to protect their seeds.
exercise: «Many berries that look tasty are poisonous.» What does poisonous mean? | Very large | Harmful, and could make you ill | *Dried in the sun | Sweet and good for you
exercise: Why are berries called healthy snacks in everyday food? | They are full of sand | *They are full of vitamin C | They make you fly | They are always poisonous
exercise: Which of these is a berry in the science meaning? | A peanut | A strawberry | A potato | *A banana
test: In «berry picking», what do people do? | Climb tall trees | *Pick berries from bushes | Bake bread at home | Swim in rivers
test: Why do birds help plants by eating berries? | They break the berries into powder | They make the seeds grow faster inside them | They keep the seeds for the winter | *They carry the seeds away and drop them far from the plant
exam: Which should you do with a berry you find outside? | Eat it straight away because it looks nice | Pick it and sell it to a friend | Taste a small piece to see how it is | *Leave it alone unless an adult who knows says it is safe
